      "description": "Watch Nottingham Forest vs Leeds highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 25, 2026. The lights of the City Ground shone brightly on August 25, 2026 , as Nottingham Forest hosted Leeds United in a high-stakes Carabao Cup encounter. Both storied clubs entered the arena with ambitions of a deep cup run, setting the stage for a tactical battle in the heart of England. Stalemate in the Opening Period The first half was a balanced affair, characterized by high pressing and missed opportunities. Leeds United carved out the better openings early on, with Lukas Nmecha and Daniel James forcing Matz Sels into action. At the other end, Nottingham Forest looked dangerous on the break, but headers from Igor Jesus and long-range efforts from Neco Williams failed to find the target. The intensity was palpable, leading to a yellow card for Ao Tanaka as both sides struggled to find a clinical edge before the interval. James Strikes After the Break The deadlock was finally broken just five minutes into the second half. Sean Longstaff turned provider, finding Daniel James in space inside the box. The winger unleashed a clinical right-footed strike into the top left corner, leaving the home crowd stunned. Forest responded with a flurry of tactical changes, introducing Callum Hudson-Odoi and Dan Ndoye to spark a comeback. Chris Wood had a golden chance to level the scoring, but James Trafford produced a world-class save to deny the veteran striker. Leeds Secure the Progression As the hosts pushed forward in search of an equalizer, they left gaps at the back that Leeds United were happy to exploit. In the 75th minute, James Justin reacted quickest to a loose ball in the six-yard box, slotting it home to double the advantage. The mountain became too steep for Nottingham Forest , whose frustrations were compounded by an injury to Neco Williams late in the game. Leeds managed the final minutes with composure, ensuring their name would be in the hat for the next round of the Carabao Cup after a professional display on the road."
